    <h1>Digital Products for Beginners</h1>

    <p>
      Digital products are products that customers can receive or use
      electronically. They can be created once and sold to multiple
      customers.
    </p>

    <h2>What Can You Create?</h2>

    <p>
      Examples include ebooks, checklists, templates, planners,
      educational guides, design resources, spreadsheets, and other
      useful digital resources.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 1 — Find a Problem</h2>

    <p>
      Think about a problem people regularly have. A good digital
      product should make something easier, faster, or more organized.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 2 — Create a Solution</h2>

    <p>
      Turn your knowledge or research into a clear and useful resource.
      Focus on providing genuine value rather than making unrealistic
      promises.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 3 — Make It Professional</h2>

    <p>
      Give your product a clear title, organize the information well,
      proofread it, and make it easy for customers to use.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 4 — Choose a Selling Platform</h2>

    <p>
      You can use a legitimate digital-commerce platform to sell and
      deliver your product. Check the platform's fees, payment options,
      and availability in your country before choosing one.
    </p>

    <h2>Step 5 — Promote Your Product</h2>

    <p>
      Create useful content related to your product and share it through
      appropriate social media or other channels where your audience is
      active.
    </p>

    <h2>Important Tip</h2>

    <p>
      Don't copy other people's products or copyrighted material.
      Create original work or use material that you have permission to use.
    </p>

